  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 311 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nSaturday through Thursday:\n\nHigh pressure lingers over the Great Lakes region through the\nweekend into early next week, gradually sinking southward into\nthe Ohio Valley by Tuesday. Expect highs around 70 degrees each\nday and lows around 50 degrees each night through Monday. Monday\nnight into Tuesday, winds turn southerly and increase as high\npressure exits and several shortwaves in the Plains phase to\ncreate a broad area of low pressure progressing eastward. Gusty\nsoutherly winds will bring highs into the low 70s. As low\npressure progresses eastward into this new airmass, thunderstorm\npotential returns to the area. Uncertainty with the strength of\nthe low remains, and therefore too early to tell any severity of\nstorms that do develop. Stay up to date with the forecast. WAA\nlingers through Tuesday night, with lows in the 60s, before a\ncold front moves through the area early Wednesday morning.\nExpect a return to highs in the 60s and lows in the low 50s\nWednesday into Thursday, with perhaps some lingering rain\nthrough Wednesday as low pressure lingers in the area.\n\nMH",
